{#-
  The assembled report (spec §15.3), adapted from SRA5's final_report.md.j2.

  Front matter is raw HTML on purpose: pandoc passes HTML blocks through
  untouched, so the masthead / KPI row / chips reach both the .html and the
  weasyprint .pdf without a custom writer.

  Three rules when editing:
   * Images use an EMPTY alt (`![](path)`). A non-empty alt makes pandoc emit a
     <figcaption>, which duplicates every caption the template already writes.
     lib/render/postprocess.py blanks any that slip in from a section draft.
   * Numeric table columns get `---:` separators. postprocess.py additionally
     detects and right-aligns numeric columns in the model-written body, so the
     whole document is consistent.
   * Body prose comes from reports/<run>/sections/*.md verbatim — every section
     already opens with its own `## N. Title`, so this file never wraps them in
     a heading of its own.
-#}
