::: {.verdict-card}
| | |
|---|---|
| **Rating** | {{ verdict.rating or 'N/A' }}{% if verdict.conviction %} <span class="chip info">{{ verdict.conviction }} conviction</span>{% endif %} |
| **Fair value** | {% if verdict.fair_value is not none %}${{ verdict.fair_value }}{% if verdict.horizon_months %} ({{ verdict.horizon_months }}-month){% endif %}{% else %}N/A{% endif %} |
| **Implied return** | {% if verdict.implied_return_pct is not none %}<span class="chip {{ verdict.return_direction }}">{{ verdict.implied_return_pct }}%</span>{% else %}N/A{% endif %} |
| **Vs. consensus** | {{ verdict.vs_consensus or 'N/A' }} |
| **Method** | {{ verdict.valuation_method or 'N/A' }} |
{% if verdict.base_case_probability is not none %}| **Base case probability** | {{ (verdict.base_case_probability * 100) | round(0) | int }}% |
{% endif %}
:::

{# No trailing period on the lead-in: report.css promotes it to a block
   uppercase kicker above the sentence, where "THESIS." reads as a typo.
   Keep this comment in the plain delimiter form. The whitespace-stripping
   variant ate the blank line above and fused the fence below with the
   verdict-card's closing colons into a six-colon opener, which nested every
   later block inside the card. And never write a nested comment delimiter in
   the text: Jinja comments do not nest, so it closes the comment early and
   spills the rest of this paragraph into the report body. #}
{% if verdict.thesis %}::: {.callout}
**Thesis** {{ verdict.thesis }}
:::
{% endif %}
{% if verdict.key_risk %}::: {.callout .caution}
**Key risk** {{ verdict.key_risk }}
:::
